---
import { FEATURES } from '../config/features.mjs';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// The newsletter section renders only while the signup is live, so the policy
// never describes processing that is not happening. Turning the flag on must
// come with a fresh LAST_UPDATED date and, once chosen, the service that
// sends the emails named as a processor.
const LAST_UPDATED = '2026-10-17';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy/' },
  ]}
  description="What personal data singletenant.ai processes, why, and your rights under UK GDPR."
>
  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="m-0 mb-2" style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Privacy policy
      </h1>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs mb-10" style="color: var(--color-mute);">
        Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}
      </p>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          singletenant.ai is operated by Simon Newton, who is the data
          controller for any personal data processed through this site.
          Contact: <a href="mailto:simon@singletenant.ai">simon@singletenant.ai</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What this site collects</h2>
        <p>
          This is a static reference site. It has no user accounts, no
          comment system{FEATURES.newsletter ? '' : ', and no newsletter'}. The site itself sets no
          cookies and runs no advertising or cross-site tracking.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Hosting logs.</strong> The site is served by Cloudflare,
          which processes visitor IP addresses and request metadata in
          transient server logs to deliver the site and protect it from
          abuse. The lawful basis is legitimate interests (UK GDPR Article
          6(1)(f)): operating and securing the service. Cloudflare acts as
          a processor; its network is global, and transfers outside the UK
          are covered by its data processing terms and standard contractual
          safeguards.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Email.</strong> If you email us (corrections, vendor
          news, press), we process your name, email address,
          and the contents of your message in order to reply. The lawful
          basis is legitimate interests (responding to correspondence you
          initiated). Correspondence is kept for as long as needed to
          handle the matter and is not added to any marketing list.
        </p>

        {FEATURES.newsletter && (
          <>
            <h2 id="newsletter">Newsletter</h2>
            <p>
              If you subscribe, we process your email address, the page you
              signed up from, and the time and wording of your consent, in
              order to send you the newsletter. The lawful basis is your
              consent (UK GDPR Article 6(1)(a)), and emails are sent only with
              that consent, as the Privacy and Electronic Communications
              Regulations require. Every email has an unsubscribe link, and
              you can also withdraw consent by emailing
              <a href="mailto:simon@singletenant.ai">simon@singletenant.ai</a>.
              Your address is kept until you unsubscribe, is not shared with
              vendors, advertisers, or sponsors, and is used for nothing else.
              Signup requests pass through Cloudflare, acting as a processor.
            </p>
          </>
        )}

        <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell or share personal data, run marketing campaigns,
          or profile visitors. Outbound links go to vendor sites which have
          their own privacy policies; referral links are marked and
          described on the <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under UK GDPR you have the right to access, rectify, or erase
          personal data we hold about you, to restrict or object to its
          processing, and to data portability. To exercise any of these,
          email <a href="mailto:simon@singletenant.ai">simon@singletenant.ai</a>.
          You also have the right to complain to the Information
          Commissioner's Office: <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          Material changes to this policy are dated at the top of this
          page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
